% ADJ52 case-27 program (this patient's observations + queries only; no rules).
% 52-year-old lifelong NON-SMOKING woman, ED with ~4 days of dry cough, exertional
% dyspnoea, pleuritic right-sided chest pain, fevers. Febrile 39.1C, tachycardic,
% SpO2 94% RA, neutrophil-predominant leucocytosis (WCC 21.4), CRP 264. CXR: dense
% RIGHT-LOWER-ZONE consolidation + blunted right costophrenic angle. Working dx:
% severe CAP with parapneumonic effusion; admitted on IV ampicillin-sulbactam.
% Diagnostic tap: EXUDATE (pleural LDH 870, protein ratio 0.6), LOW glucose,
% LYMPHOCYTE-RICH, pleural ADA 18.6 U/L (BELOW the 40 U/L TB cutoff). All cultures
% (fluid, blood, sputum) and bronchial washings NEGATIVE. Despite a full IV
% antibiotic course the opacity did NOT clear; empirical 6-month anti-TB started on
% presumption of occult TB. Patient remained relatively well (intermittent low-grade
% fever/cough). CT thorax at 2 and 6 months: SAME band of RLL consolidative opacity,
% essentially UNCHANGED, NO cavitation, NO response to antibacterial OR anti-TB.
% Transbronchial biopsy: ATYPICAL LYMPHOID CELLS. CT-guided core biopsy, upper-GI
% endoscopy with gastric biopsies, and bone-marrow trephine arranged.

% --- the indolent-lymphoid gestalt (one correlated syndrome) ---
observe histology(atypical_lymphoid_cells_on_lung_tissue)
observe pleural_fluid(lymphocyte_rich)
observe clinical_course(indolent_relatively_well)
observe staging_workup(other_mucosal_and_marrow_sites)

% --- the non-resolution-despite-therapy gestalt (one correlated syndrome) ---
observe consolidation_course(unchanged_over_months)
observe treatment_response(no_response_to_antibiotics)
observe treatment_response(no_response_to_anti_tb)

% --- pleural fluid character and microbiology ---
observe pleural_fluid(exudate_high_ldh)
observe pleural_ada(below_tb_cutoff)
observe microbiology(persistently_culture_negative)

% --- imaging and presentation ---
observe imaging(no_cavitation)
observe presentation(acute_febrile_neutrophilic_lobar)

